IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc21-nouns`
IMPORT `ccc21-part-19-absolute`

-- ccc21-part-18.l4 -- PART XVIII, Procedure on Preliminary Inquiry, ss 535 to 551 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Imports the keel's core, this part's nouns, and section 552 and 553 (absolute jurisdiction) from ccc21-part-19-absolute.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); not the official text.
-- How a result reads: JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words: each such branch carries `-- FALSE-kind (...): "<quote>"`); NOTHING (not covered: `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`).
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. `-- GRANT-GATE: ...` and `-- CLAIM-NAMED` mark the groups NOTES.md counts for a lawyer (see ccc21-part-17.l4's header).
-- Seams this part takes as inputs (PLAN.md section 6): `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` and `s 577 a direct indictment has been preferred`, each a MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- that is carried through as NOTHING when it is NOTHING. A "who is before whom" fact is a small enumeration because the text distinguishes a justice who is a provincial court judge from one who is not.

§ `PART XVIII -- Procedure on Preliminary Inquiry`

§§ `Section 535 -- Inquiry by justice`

-- "punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment" (ss 535, 536(2), 536(2.1), 536.1(2), 536.1(2.1), 553-related, 568-569 use the period): is the most the indictable limb allows 14 years or more?
-- "Imprisonment for life" is more than 14 years; a term is compared with 14 years in years, months, days, and "less a day" takes a day off (14 years less a day is below 14 years).
-- src:11882 | 535 If an accused who is charged with an indictable offence that is punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment is before a justice and a request has been made for a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536(4) or 536.1(3), the justice shall, in accordance with this Part, inquire into the charge and any other indictable offence, in respect of the same transaction, founded on the facts that are disclosed by the evidence taken in accordance with this Part.
@ref s 535 (src:11882-11882)
GIVEN `the maximum imprisonment for the offence` IS AN Imprisonment
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 535 an offence punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the maximum imprisonment for the offence`
    WHEN `no imprisonment is stated` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section that creates the offence states the maximum, and none is given here
    WHEN `imprisonment for life` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `imprisonment for a term of` term THEN
        IF `term is above 14 years` OR ((NOT term's `less a day`) AND `term is exactly 14 years`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment"
        WHERE
            `term is above 14 years` MEANS
                term's years GREATER THAN 14 OR (term's years EQUALS 14 AND (term's months GREATER THAN 0 OR (term's months EQUALS 0 AND term's days GREATER THAN 0)))
            `term is exactly 14 years` MEANS
                term's years EQUALS 14 AND term's months EQUALS 0 AND term's days EQUALS 0

-- "an indictable offence": the class of the offence is indictable; the core's third class (both indictable and punishable on summary conviction) is an indictable offence
-- when the prosecutor proceeds by indictment (the text says nothing of that: NOTES.md fork F4).
-- src:11882 | 535 If an accused who is charged with an indictable offence that is punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment is before a justice and a request has been made for a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536(4) or 536.1(3), the justice shall, in accordance with this Part, inquire into the charge and any other indictable offence, in respect of the same transaction, founded on the facts that are disclosed by the evidence taken in accordance with this Part.
@ref s 535 (src:11882-11882)
GIVEN charge IS A `s 535 the charge`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 535 the offence charged is an indictable offence` MEANS
        charge's `s 535 the class of the offence charged` EQUALS `an indictable offence`
    OR (    charge's `s 535 the class of the offence charged` EQUALS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
        AND charge's `s 535 the mode in which the prosecutor proceeds` EQUALS `by indictment`)

-- 535 If an accused who is charged with an indictable offence that is punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment is before a justice and a request has been made for a preliminary inquiry
-- under subsection 536(4) or 536.1(3), the justice shall, in accordance with this Part, inquire into the charge and any other indictable offence, in respect of the same transaction, founded on the facts disclosed by the evidence.
-- src:11882 | 535 If an accused who is charged with an indictable offence that is punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment is before a justice and a request has been made for a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536(4) or 536.1(3), the justice shall, in accordance with this Part, inquire into the charge and any other indictable offence, in respect of the same transaction, founded on the facts that are disclosed by the evidence taken in accordance with this Part.
@ref s 535 (src:11882-11882)
GIVEN charge IS A `s 535 the charge`
      `the accused is before a justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a request has been made for a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536(4) or 536.1(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 535 the justice shall inquire into the charge` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `s 535 the offence charged is an indictable offence` charge THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an accused who is charged with an indictable offence"
        IF `fourteen years or more` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that is punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment"
        IF NOT `the accused is before a justice` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is before a justice"
        IF NOT `a request has been made for a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536(4) or 536.1(3)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a request has been made for a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536(4) or 536.1(3)"
        IF `fourteen years or more` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the maximum imprisonment for the offence is not stated
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `fourteen years or more` MEANS `s 535 an offence punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment` (charge's `s 535 the maximum imprisonment for the offence on indictment`)

-- 535 ... and any other indictable offence, in respect of the same transaction, founded on the facts that are disclosed by the evidence taken in accordance with this Part.
-- src:11882 | 535 If an accused who is charged with an indictable offence that is punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment is before a justice and a request has been made for a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536(4) or 536.1(3), the justice shall, in accordance with this Part, inquire into the charge and any other indictable offence, in respect of the same transaction, founded on the facts that are disclosed by the evidence taken in accordance with this Part.
@ref s 535 (src:11882-11882)
GIVEN `the answer of s 535 the justice shall inquire into the charge` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the other offence is an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other offence is in respect of the same transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other offence is founded on the facts that are disclosed by the evidence taken in accordance with this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 535 the inquiry extends to the other indictable offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer of s 535 the justice shall inquire into the charge`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the justice inquires into the charge at all is not settled
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an accused who is charged with an indictable offence"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the other offence is an indictable offence` AND `the other offence is in respect of the same transaction` AND `the other offence is founded on the facts that are disclosed by the evidence taken in accordance with this Part`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any other indictable offence, in respect of the same transaction, founded on the facts that are disclosed by the evidence"

§§ `Section 536 -- Remand by justice to provincial court judge in certain cases`

-- Who the accused is before, as section 536 distinguishes them: a justice (other than a provincial court judge, or a provincial court judge), or someone who is not a justice.
-- src:11884 | 536 (1) Where an accused is before a justice other than a provincial court judge charged with an offence over which a provincial court judge has absolute jurisdiction under section 553, the justice shall remand the accused to appear before a provincial court judge having jurisdiction in the territorial division in which the offence is alleged to have been committed.
@ref s 536(1) (src:11884-11884)
DECLARE `s 536(1) who the accused is before` IS ONE OF
    `s 536(1) a justice other than a provincial court judge`
    `s 536(1) a provincial court judge`
    `s 536(1) someone who is not a justice`

-- 536 (1) Where an accused is before a justice other than a provincial court judge charged with an offence over which a provincial court judge has absolute jurisdiction under section 553,
-- the justice shall remand the accused to appear before a provincial court judge having jurisdiction in the territorial division in which the offence is alleged to have been committed.
-- src:11884 | 536 (1) Where an accused is before a justice other than a provincial court judge charged with an offence over which a provincial court judge has absolute jurisdiction under section 553, the justice shall remand the accused to appear before a provincial court judge having jurisdiction in the territorial division in which the offence is alleged to have been committed.
@ref s 536(1) (src:11884-11884)
GIVEN charge IS A `s 535 the charge`
      `who the accused is before` IS A `s 536(1) who the accused is before`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 536(1) the justice shall remand the accused to appear before a provincial court judge` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`who the accused is before` EQUALS `s 536(1) a justice other than a provincial court judge`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an accused is before a justice other than a provincial court judge"
        IF NOT (`s 553 the offence is within the absolute jurisdiction of a provincial court judge` (charge's `s 535 the facts that bear on absolute jurisdiction`) EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "charged with an offence over which a provincial court judge has absolute jurisdiction under section 553"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 536 (2) If an accused is before a justice, charged with an indictable offence that is punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment, other than an offence listed in section 469 ...
-- Who "an accused referred to in subsection (2)" is: before a justice, charged with an indictable offence punishable by 14 years or more, other than one listed in section 469.
-- src:11886 | (2) If an accused is before a justice, charged with an indictable offence that is punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment, other than an offence listed in section 469, the justice shall, after the information has been read to the accused, put the accused to an election in the following words:
@ref s 536(2) (src:11886-11886)
GIVEN charge IS A `s 535 the charge`
      `who the accused is before` IS A `s 536(1) who the accused is before`
      `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 536(2) the accused is one referred to in subsection (2)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `who the accused is before` EQUALS `s 536(1) someone who is not a justice` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an accused is before a justice"
        IF NOT `s 535 the offence charged is an indictable offence` charge THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "charged with an indictable offence"
        IF `fourteen years or more` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that is punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment"
        IF `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than an offence listed in section 469"
        IF `fourteen years or more` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the maximum imprisonment for the offence is not stated
        IF `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the offence is listed in section 469 is for that section
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `fourteen years or more` MEANS `s 535 an offence punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment` (charge's `s 535 the maximum imprisonment for the offence on indictment`)

-- 536 (2) ... the justice shall, after the information has been read to the accused, put the accused to an election in the following words: (the words)
-- src:11887 | You have the option to elect to be tried by a provincial court judge without a jury and without having had a preliminary inquiry; or you may elect to be tried by a judge without a jury; or you may elect to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury. If you do not elect now, you are deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury. If you elect to be tried by a judge without a jury or by a court composed of a judge and jury or if you are deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury, you will have a preliminary inquiry only if you or the prosecutor requests one. How do you elect to be tried?
@ref s 536(2) (src:11887-11887)
`s 536(2) the words in which the justice puts the accused to an election` MEANS "You have the option to elect to be tried by a provincial court judge without a jury and without having had a preliminary inquiry; or you may elect to be tried by a judge without a jury; or you may elect to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury. If you do not elect now, you are deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury. If you elect to be tried by a judge without a jury or by a court composed of a judge and jury or if you are deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury, you will have a preliminary inquiry only if you or the prosecutor requests one. How do you elect to be tried?"

-- src:11886 | (2) If an accused is before a justice, charged with an indictable offence that is punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment, other than an offence listed in section 469, the justice shall, after the information has been read to the accused, put the accused to an election in the following words:
@ref s 536(2) (src:11886-11886)
GIVEN `the answer of s 536(2) the accused is one referred to in subsection (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the information has been read to the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 536(2) the justice shall put the accused to an election in the words of subsection (2)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the answer of s 536(2) the accused is one referred to in subsection (2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an accused is before a justice, charged with an indictable offence that is punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment"
        IF NOT `the information has been read to the accused` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "after the information has been read to the accused"
        IF `the answer of s 536(2) the accused is one referred to in subsection (2)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the accused is one referred to in subsection (2) is not settled
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 536 (2.1) If an accused is before a justice, charged with an indictable offence -- other than an offence that is punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment, an offence listed in section 469 that is not
-- punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment or an offence over which a provincial court judge has absolute jurisdiction under section 553 --, the justice shall, after the information has been read, put the accused to an election.
-- src:11889 | (2.1) If an accused is before a justice, charged with an indictable offence — other than an offence that is punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment, an offence listed in section 469 that is not punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment or an offence over which a provincial court judge has absolute jurisdiction under section 553 —, the justice shall, after the information has been read to the accused, put the accused to an election in the following words:
@ref s 536(2.1) (src:11889-11889)
GIVEN charge IS A `s 535 the charge`
      `who the accused is before` IS A `s 536(1) who the accused is before`
      `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 536(2.1) the accused is one referred to in subsection (2.1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `who the accused is before` EQUALS `s 536(1) someone who is not a justice` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an accused is before a justice"
        IF NOT `s 535 the offence charged is an indictable offence` charge THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "charged with an indictable offence"
        IF `fourteen years or more` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than an offence that is punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment"
        IF `listed in 469 and not 14 years or more` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an offence listed in section 469 that is not punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment"
        IF `absolute jurisdiction` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an offence over which a provincial court judge has absolute jurisdiction under section 553"
        IF `fourteen years or more` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the maximum imprisonment for the offence is not stated
        IF `listed in 469 and not 14 years or more` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the offence is listed in section 469 is for that section
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `fourteen years or more` MEANS `s 535 an offence punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment` (charge's `s 535 the maximum imprisonment for the offence on indictment`)
        `listed in 469 and not 14 years or more` MEANS `s 535 three-valued and` `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`s 535 three-valued not` `fourteen years or more`)
        `absolute jurisdiction` MEANS `s 553 the offence is within the absolute jurisdiction of a provincial court judge` (charge's `s 535 the facts that bear on absolute jurisdiction`) EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- src:11890 | You have the option to elect to be tried by a provincial court judge without a jury; or you may elect to be tried by a judge without a jury; or you may elect to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury. If you do not elect now, you are deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury. How do you elect to be tried?
@ref s 536(2.1) (src:11890-11890)
`s 536(2.1) the words in which the justice puts the accused to an election` MEANS "You have the option to elect to be tried by a provincial court judge without a jury; or you may elect to be tried by a judge without a jury; or you may elect to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury. If you do not elect now, you are deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury. How do you elect to be tried?"

-- src:11889 | (2.1) If an accused is before a justice, charged with an indictable offence — other than an offence that is punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment, an offence listed in section 469 that is not punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment or an offence over which a provincial court judge has absolute jurisdiction under section 553 —, the justice shall, after the information has been read to the accused, put the accused to an election in the following words:
@ref s 536(2.1) (src:11889-11889)
GIVEN `the answer of s 536(2.1) the accused is one referred to in subsection (2.1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the information has been read to the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 536(2.1) the justice shall put the accused to an election in the words of subsection (2.1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the answer of s 536(2.1) the accused is one referred to in subsection (2.1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an accused is before a justice, charged with an indictable offence"
        IF NOT `the information has been read to the accused` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "after the information has been read to the accused"
        IF `the answer of s 536(2.1) the accused is one referred to in subsection (2.1)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the accused is one referred to in subsection (2.1) is not settled
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 536 (3) Where an accused elects to be tried by a provincial court judge, the justice shall endorse on the information a record of the election and shall (a) where the justice is not a provincial court judge,
-- remand the accused to appear and plead to the charge before a provincial court judge having jurisdiction ...; or (b) where the justice is a provincial court judge, call on the accused to plead to the charge and if the
-- accused does not plead guilty, proceed with the trial or fix a time for the trial.
-- src:11892 | (3) Where an accused elects to be tried by a provincial court judge, the justice shall endorse on the information a record of the election and shall
@ref s 536(3) (src:11892-11892)
GIVEN `the accused's answer` IS A `s 536(2) the accused's answer when put to an election`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 536(3) the accused elects to be tried by a provincial court judge` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the accused's answer`
    WHEN `s 536(2) elects` mode THEN mode EQUALS `s 536(2) trial by a provincial court judge`
    WHEN `s 536(2) does not elect` THEN FALSE

-- src:11892 | (3) Where an accused elects to be tried by a provincial court judge, the justice shall endorse on the information a record of the election and shall
@ref s 536(3) (src:11892-11892)
GIVEN `the accused's answer` IS A `s 536(2) the accused's answer when put to an election`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 536(3) the justice shall endorse on the information a record of the election` MEANS
    IF `s 536(3) the accused elects to be tried by a provincial court judge` `the accused's answer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an accused elects to be tried by a provincial court judge"

-- src:11893 | (a) where the justice is not a provincial court judge, remand the accused to appear and plead to the charge before a provincial court judge having jurisdiction in the territorial division in which the offence is alleged to have been committed; or
@ref s 536(3)(a) (src:11893-11893)
GIVEN `the accused's answer` IS A `s 536(2) the accused's answer when put to an election`
      `who the accused is before` IS A `s 536(1) who the accused is before`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 536(3)(a) the justice shall remand the accused to appear and plead before a provincial court judge` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `s 536(3) the accused elects to be tried by a provincial court judge` `the accused's answer` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an accused elects to be tried by a provincial court judge"
        IF `who the accused is before` EQUALS `s 536(1) a provincial court judge` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the justice is not a provincial court judge"
        IF `who the accused is before` EQUALS `s 536(1) someone who is not a justice` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the justice" is the one before whom the accused elects, and none is given
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:11894 | (b) where the justice is a provincial court judge, call on the accused to plead to the charge and if the accused does not plead guilty, proceed with the trial or fix a time for the trial.
@ref s 536(3)(b) (src:11894-11894)
GIVEN `the accused's answer` IS A `s 536(2) the accused's answer when put to an election`
      `who the accused is before` IS A `s 536(1) who the accused is before`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 536(3)(b) the provincial court judge shall call on the accused to plead to the charge` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `s 536(3) the accused elects to be tried by a provincial court judge` `the accused's answer` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an accused elects to be tried by a provincial court judge"
        IF `who the accused is before` EQUALS `s 536(1) a justice other than a provincial court judge` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the justice is a provincial court judge"
        IF `who the accused is before` EQUALS `s 536(1) someone who is not a justice` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the justice" is the one before whom the accused elects, and none is given
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:11894 | (b) where the justice is a provincial court judge, call on the accused to plead to the charge and if the accused does not plead guilty, proceed with the trial or fix a time for the trial.
@ref s 536(3)(b) (src:11894-11894)
GIVEN `the answer of s 536(3)(b) the provincial court judge shall call on the accused to plead` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the accused pleads guilty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 536(3)(b) the provincial court judge shall proceed with the trial or fix a time for the trial` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer of s 536(3)(b) the provincial court judge shall call on the accused to plead`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the provincial court judge calls on the accused to plead is not settled
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the justice is a provincial court judge"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the accused pleads guilty`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the accused does not plead guilty"
        ELSE JUST TRUE

-- 536 (4) If an accused referred to in subsection (2) elects to be tried by a judge without a jury or by a court composed of a judge and jury or does not elect when put to the election or is deemed under paragraph 565(1)(a)
-- to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury, or if an accused is charged with an offence listed in section 469 that is punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment, the justice shall, subject to section 577,
-- on the request of the accused or the prosecutor made at that time or within the period fixed by rules of court made under section 482 or 482.1 or, if there are no such rules, by the justice, hold a preliminary inquiry into the charge.
-- src:11896 | (4) If an accused referred to in subsection (2) elects to be tried by a judge without a jury or by a court composed of a judge and jury or does not elect when put to the election or is deemed under paragraph 565(1)(a) to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury, or if an accused is charged with an offence listed in section 469 that is punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment, the justice shall, subject to section 577, on the request of the accused or the prosecutor made at that time or within the period fixed by rules of court made under section 482 or 482.1 or, if there are no such rules, by the justice, hold a preliminary inquiry into the charge.
@ref s 536(4) (src:11896-11896)
GIVEN `the accused's answer` IS A `s 536(2) the accused's answer when put to an election`
      `the accused is deemed under paragraph 565(1)(a) to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 536(4) the accused elects a judge without a jury or a judge and jury, or does not elect, or is deemed under paragraph 565(1)(a) to have elected a judge and jury` MEANS
        `the accused is deemed under paragraph 565(1)(a) to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury`
    OR  CONSIDER `the accused's answer`
        WHEN `s 536(2) elects` mode THEN NOT (mode EQUALS `s 536(2) trial by a provincial court judge`)
        WHEN `s 536(2) does not elect` THEN TRUE

-- src:11896 | (4) If an accused referred to in subsection (2) elects to be tried by a judge without a jury or by a court composed of a judge and jury or does not elect when put to the election or is deemed under paragraph 565(1)(a) to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury, or if an accused is charged with an offence listed in section 469 that is punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment, the justice shall, subject to section 577, on the request of the accused or the prosecutor made at that time or within the period fixed by rules of court made under section 482 or 482.1 or, if there are no such rules, by the justice, hold a preliminary inquiry into the charge.
@ref s 536(4) (src:11896-11896)
GIVEN charge IS A `s 535 the charge`
      `who the accused is before` IS A `s 536(1) who the accused is before`
      `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the accused's answer` IS A `s 536(2) the accused's answer when put to an election`
      `the accused is deemed under paragraph 565(1)(a) to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused or the prosecutor made a request for a preliminary inquiry at that time or within the period fixed by rules of court made under section 482 or 482.1 or, if there are no such rules, by the justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 577 a direct indictment has been preferred` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 536(4) the justice shall hold a preliminary inquiry into the charge` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the first limb` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `the second limb` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an accused referred to in subsection (2) elects to be tried by a judge without a jury"
        IF NOT `the accused or the prosecutor made a request for a preliminary inquiry at that time or within the period fixed by rules of court made under section 482 or 482.1 or, if there are no such rules, by the justice` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on the request of the accused or the prosecutor made at that time or within the period fixed by rules of court made under section 482 or 482.1"
        IF `the first limb` EQUALS NOTHING AND NOT (`the second limb` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the accused is one referred to in subsection (2) turns on section 469 or on a maximum that is not stated
        IF `the second limb` EQUALS NOTHING AND NOT (`the first limb` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the offence is listed in section 469 is for that section
        IF `s 577 a direct indictment has been preferred` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "subject to section 577"
        IF `s 577 a direct indictment has been preferred` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "subject to section 577"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `the first limb` MEANS
            `s 535 three-valued and` (`s 536(2) the accused is one referred to in subsection (2)` charge `who the accused is before` `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469`)
                (JUST (`s 536(4) the accused elects a judge without a jury or a judge and jury, or does not elect, or is deemed under paragraph 565(1)(a) to have elected a judge and jury` `the accused's answer` `the accused is deemed under paragraph 565(1)(a) to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury`))
        `the second limb` MEANS
            `s 535 three-valued and` `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`s 535 an offence punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment` (charge's `s 535 the maximum imprisonment for the offence on indictment`))

