§§ `Section 536.1 -- Remand by justice -- Nunavut`

-- Who the accused is before, as section 536.1 distinguishes them: a justice of the peace, a judge, or neither.
-- src:11912 | 536.1 (1) If an accused is before a justice of the peace charged with an indictable offence mentioned in section 553, the justice of the peace shall remand the accused to appear before a judge.
@ref s 536.1(1) (src:11912-11912)
DECLARE `s 536.1(1) who the accused is before` IS ONE OF
    `s 536.1(1) a justice of the peace`
    `s 536.1(1) a judge`
    `s 536.1(1) someone who is neither a justice of the peace nor a judge`

-- 536.1 (1) If an accused is before a justice of the peace charged with an indictable offence mentioned in section 553, the justice of the peace shall remand the accused to appear before a judge.
-- src:11912 | 536.1 (1) If an accused is before a justice of the peace charged with an indictable offence mentioned in section 553, the justice of the peace shall remand the accused to appear before a judge.
@ref s 536.1(1) (src:11912-11912)
GIVEN charge IS A `s 535 the charge`
      `who the accused is before` IS A `s 536.1(1) who the accused is before`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 536.1(1) the justice of the peace shall remand the accused to appear before a judge` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`who the accused is before` EQUALS `s 536.1(1) a justice of the peace`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an accused is before a justice of the peace"
        IF NOT `s 535 the offence charged is an indictable offence` charge THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "charged with an indictable offence mentioned in section 553"
        IF NOT (`s 553 the offence is within the absolute jurisdiction of a provincial court judge` (charge's `s 535 the facts that bear on absolute jurisdiction`) EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an indictable offence mentioned in section 553"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

