        IF NOT `s 535 the offence charged is an indictable offence` charge THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "charged with an indictable offence"
        IF `fourteen years or more` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that is punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment"
        IF `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than an offence mentioned in section 469"
        IF `fourteen years or more` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the maximum imprisonment for the offence is not stated
        IF `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the offence is mentioned in section 469 is for that section
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `fourteen years or more` MEANS `s 535 an offence punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment` (charge's `s 535 the maximum imprisonment for the offence on indictment`)

-- src:11915 | You have the option to elect to be tried by a judge without a jury or to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury. If you do not elect now, you are deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury. If you elect to be tried by a judge without a jury or by a court composed of a judge and jury or if you are deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury, you will have a preliminary inquiry only if you or the prosecutor requests one. How do you elect to be tried?
@ref s 536.1(2) (src:11915-11915)
`s 536.1(2) the words in which the judge or justice of the peace puts the accused to an election` MEANS "You have the option to elect to be tried by a judge without a jury or to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury. If you do not elect now, you are deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury. If you elect to be tried by a judge without a jury or by a court composed of a judge and jury or if you are deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury, you will have a preliminary inquiry only if you or the prosecutor requests one. How do you elect to be tried?"

