-- 536.1 (3) If an accused referred to in subsection (2) elects to be tried by a judge without a jury or by a court composed of a judge and jury or does not elect ... or is deemed under paragraph 565(1)(a) ..., or if an accused is charged with
-- an offence listed in section 469 that is punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment, the justice or judge shall, subject to section 577, on the request of the accused or the prosecutor made at that time or within the period fixed ..., hold a preliminary inquiry.
-- src:11920 | (3) If an accused referred to in subsection (2) elects to be tried by a judge without a jury or by a court composed of a judge and jury or does not elect when put to the election or is deemed under paragraph 565(1)(a) to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury or if an accused is charged with an offence listed in section 469 that is punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment, the justice or judge shall, subject to section 577, on the request of the accused or the prosecutor made at that time or within the period fixed by rules of court made under section 482 or 482.1 or, if there are no such rules, by the judge or justice, hold a preliminary inquiry into the charge.
@ref s 536.1(3) (src:11920-11920)
GIVEN charge IS A `s 535 the charge`
      `who the accused is before` IS A `s 536.1(1) who the accused is before`
      `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
