      `the accused is deemed under paragraph 565(1)(a) to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused or the prosecutor made a request for a preliminary inquiry at that time or within the period fixed by rules of court made under section 482 or 482.1 or, if there are no such rules, by the judge or justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 577 a direct indictment has been preferred` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 536.1(3) the justice or judge shall hold a preliminary inquiry into the charge` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the first limb` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `the second limb` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an accused referred to in subsection (2) elects to be tried by a judge without a jury"
        IF NOT `the accused or the prosecutor made a request for a preliminary inquiry at that time or within the period fixed by rules of court made under section 482 or 482.1 or, if there are no such rules, by the judge or justice` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on the request of the accused or the prosecutor made at that time or within the period fixed by rules of court made under section 482 or 482.1"
        IF `the first limb` EQUALS NOTHING AND NOT (`the second limb` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the accused is one referred to in subsection (2) turns on section 469 or on a maximum that is not stated
        IF `the second limb` EQUALS NOTHING AND NOT (`the first limb` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the offence is listed in section 469 is for that section
        IF `s 577 a direct indictment has been preferred` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "subject to section 577"
        IF `s 577 a direct indictment has been preferred` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "subject to section 577"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `the first limb` MEANS
            `s 535 three-valued and` (`s 536.1(2) the accused is one referred to in subsection (2)` charge `who the accused is before` `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469`)
                (JUST (`s 536(4) the accused elects a judge without a jury or a judge and jury, or does not elect, or is deemed under paragraph 565(1)(a) to have elected a judge and jury` `the accused's answer` `the accused is deemed under paragraph 565(1)(a) to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury`))
        `the second limb` MEANS
            `s 535 three-valued and` `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`s 535 an offence punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment` (charge's `s 535 the maximum imprisonment for the offence on indictment`))

