-- 536.4 (1) The justice before whom a preliminary inquiry is to be held may order, on application of the prosecutor or the accused or on the justice's own motion, that a hearing be held, within the period fixed by rules of court
-- made under section 482 or 482.1 or, if there are no such rules, by the justice, to (a) assist the parties to identify the issues; (b) assist the parties to identify the witnesses; and (c) encourage the parties to consider any other matters that would promote a fair and expeditious inquiry.
