§§ `Section 538 -- Organization`

-- 538 Where an accused is an organization, subsections 556(1) and (2) apply with such modifications as the circumstances require.
-- src:11986 | 538 Where an accused is an organization, subsections 556(1) and (2) apply with such modifications as the circumstances require.
@ref s 538 (src:11986-11986)
GIVEN `s 2 organization: the accused is an organization` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 538 subsections 556(1) and (2) apply to the accused with such modifications as the circumstances require` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2 organization: the accused is an organization`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the accused is an organization is for section 2
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an accused is an organization"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE

§§ `Section 539 -- Order restricting publication of evidence taken at preliminary inquiry`

-- 539 (1) Prior to the commencement of the taking of evidence at a preliminary inquiry, the justice holding the inquiry (a) may, if application therefor is made by the prosecutor, and (b) shall, if application therefor is made by any of the accused,
-- make an order directing that the evidence taken at the inquiry shall not be published in any document or broadcast or transmitted in any way before such time as, in respect of each of the accused, (c) he or she is discharged, or (d) if he or she is ordered to stand trial, the trial is ended.
-- src:11990 | 539 (1) Prior to the commencement of the taking of evidence at a preliminary inquiry, the justice holding the inquiry
-- src:11991 | (a) may, if application therefor is made by the prosecutor, and
@ref s 539(1)(a) (src:11990-11991)
GIVEN `the application is made by the prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made before the commencement of the taking of evidence at the preliminary inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 539(1)(a) the justice may make an order restricting publication of the evidence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the application is made before the commencement of the taking of evidence at the preliminary inquiry` THEN JUST FALSE   -- GRANT-GATE: where/when/upon/period -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Prior to the commencement of the taking of evidence at a preliminary inquiry"
        IF NOT `the application is made by the prosecutor` THEN NOTHING   -- GRANT-GATE: if -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if application therefor is made by the prosecutor"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:11990 | 539 (1) Prior to the commencement of the taking of evidence at a preliminary inquiry, the justice holding the inquiry
-- src:11991 | (a) may, if application therefor is made by the prosecutor, and
-- src:11992 | (b) shall, if application therefor is made by any of the accused,
@ref s 539(1)(b) (src:11990-11992)
GIVEN `the application is made by any of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made before the commencement of the taking of evidence at the preliminary inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 539(1)(b) the justice shall make an order restricting publication of the evidence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the application is made before the commencement of the taking of evidence at the preliminary inquiry` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Prior to the commencement of the taking of evidence at a preliminary inquiry"
        IF NOT `the application is made by any of the accused` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if application therefor is made by any of the accused"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The order bars publication "before such time as ... (c) he or she is discharged, or (d) if he or she is ordered to stand trial, the trial is ended": an "until" bar (ruling (d) of 2026-11-05): JUST TRUE before that time, JUST FALSE after it.
-- src:11993 | make an order directing that the evidence taken at the inquiry shall not be published in any document or broadcast or transmitted in any way before such time as, in respect of each of the accused,
-- src:11994 | (c) he or she is discharged, or
-- src:11995 | (d) if he or she is ordered to stand trial, the trial is ended.
@ref s 539(1)(c) and (d) (src:11993-11995)
GIVEN `an order was made under subsection 539(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused has been discharged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused has been ordered to stand trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trial has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 539(1) the order bars publication of the evidence taken at the inquiry` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `an order was made under subsection 539(1)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "make an order directing that the evidence taken at the inquiry shall not be published"
        IF `the accused has been discharged` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "he or she is discharged"
        IF `the accused has been ordered to stand trial` AND `the trial has ended` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if he or she is ordered to stand trial, the trial is ended"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 539 (2) Where an accused is not represented by counsel at a preliminary inquiry, the justice holding the inquiry shall, prior to the commencement of the taking of evidence at the inquiry, inform the accused of his right to make application under subsection (1).
-- src:11997 | (2) Where an accused is not represented by counsel at a preliminary inquiry, the justice holding the inquiry shall, prior to the commencement of the taking of evidence at the inquiry, inform the accused of his right to make application under subsection (1).
@ref s 539(2) (src:11997-11997)
GIVEN `the accused is represented by counsel at the preliminary inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the taking of evidence at the inquiry has commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 539(2) the justice shall inform the accused of the right to apply for an order restricting publication` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the accused is represented by counsel at the preliminary inquiry` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an accused is not represented by counsel at a preliminary inquiry"
        IF `the taking of evidence at the inquiry has commenced` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "prior to the commencement of the taking of evidence at the inquiry"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 539 (3) Every one who fails to comply with an order made pursuant to subsection (1) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
-- src:11999 | (3) Every one who fails to comply with an order made pursuant to subsection (1) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 539(3) (src:11999-11999)
GIVEN `an order was made pursuant to subsection 539(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fails to comply with it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 539(3) the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` MEANS
    IF `an order was made pursuant to subsection 539(1)` AND `the person fails to comply with it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one who fails to comply with an order made pursuant to subsection (1)"

-- The class and the punishment the section states for that offence: summary conviction, and no maximum stated (the general summary-conviction punishment is another Part's).
-- src:11999 | (3) Every one who fails to comply with an order made pursuant to subsection (1) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 539(3) (src:11999-11999)
`s 539(3) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:11999 | (3) Every one who fails to comply with an order made pursuant to subsection (1) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 539(3) (src:11999-11999)
`s 539(3) the punishment the section states` MEANS
    Punishment WITH
        `mode` IS `on summary conviction`
        `maximum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`
        `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`
        `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`
        `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`

-- 539 (4) [Repealed, 2005, c. 32, s. 18]: the text shows
-- src:12000 | (4) [Repealed, 2005, c. 32, s. 18]
@ref s 539(4) (src:12000-12000)
`s 539(4) repealed` MEANS "(4) [Repealed, 2005, c. 32, s. 18]"

§§ `Section 540 -- Taking evidence`

-- 540 (1) Where an accused is before a justice holding a preliminary inquiry, the justice shall (a) take the evidence under oath of the witnesses called on the part of the prosecution, subject to subsection 537(1.01), and allow the accused or counsel for the accused to cross-examine them;
-- src:12002 | 540 (1) Where an accused is before a justice holding a preliminary inquiry, the justice shall
-- src:12003 | (a) take the evidence under oath of the witnesses called on the part of the prosecution, subject to subsection 537(1.01), and allow the accused or counsel for the accused to cross-examine them; and
@ref s 540(1)(a) (src:12002-12003)
GIVEN `the accused is before a justice holding a preliminary inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice has limited the witnesses to be heard under subsection 537(1.01)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 540(1)(a) the justice shall take the evidence of the prosecution witnesses under oath and allow the accused or counsel to cross-examine them` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the accused is before a justice holding a preliminary inquiry` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an accused is before a justice holding a preliminary inquiry"
        IF `the justice has limited the witnesses to be heard under subsection 537(1.01)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to subsection 537(1.01)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (b) cause a record of the evidence of each witness to be taken (i) in legible writing in the form of a deposition, in Form 31, or by a stenographer appointed by him or pursuant to law, or (ii) in a province where a sound recording apparatus
-- is authorized by or under provincial legislation for use in civil cases, by the type of apparatus so authorized and in accordance with the requirements of the provincial legislation.
-- src:12004 | (b) cause a record of the evidence of each witness to be taken
-- src:12005 | (i) in legible writing in the form of a deposition, in Form 31, or by a stenographer appointed by him or pursuant to law, or
-- src:12006 | (ii) in a province where a sound recording apparatus is authorized by or under provincial legislation for use in civil cases, by the type of apparatus so authorized and in accordance with the requirements of the provincial legislation.
@ref s 540(1)(b) (src:12004-12006)
DECLARE `s 540(1)(b) how the record of the evidence of a witness is taken` IS ONE OF
    `s 540(1)(b)(i) in legible writing in the form of a deposition, in Form 31, or by a stenographer appointed by the justice or pursuant to law`
    `s 540(1)(b)(ii) by the type of sound recording apparatus authorized by or under provincial legislation for use in civil cases`
    `s 540(1)(b) any other way`

-- src:12004 | (b) cause a record of the evidence of each witness to be taken
-- src:12005 | (i) in legible writing in the form of a deposition, in Form 31, or by a stenographer appointed by him or pursuant to law, or
-- src:12006 | (ii) in a province where a sound recording apparatus is authorized by or under provincial legislation for use in civil cases, by the type of apparatus so authorized and in accordance with the requirements of the provincial legislation.
@ref s 540(1)(b) (src:12004-12006)
GIVEN `the accused is before a justice holding a preliminary inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN
      `how the record is taken` IS A `s 540(1)(b) how the record of the evidence of a witness is taken`
      `a sound recording apparatus is authorized in the province by or under provincial legislation for use in civil cases` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 540(1)(b) the justice shall cause a record of the evidence of each witness to be taken in the way the paragraph allows` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the accused is before a justice holding a preliminary inquiry` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an accused is before a justice holding a preliminary inquiry"
        IF `how the record is taken` EQUALS `s 540(1)(b) any other way` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "cause a record of the evidence of each witness to be taken (i) in legible writing"
        IF `how the record is taken` EQUALS `s 540(1)(b)(ii) by the type of sound recording apparatus authorized by or under provincial legislation for use in civil cases` AND NOT `a sound recording apparatus is authorized in the province by or under provincial legislation for use in civil cases` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in a province where a sound recording apparatus is authorized by or under provincial legislation for use in civil cases"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 540 (2) Where a deposition is taken down in writing, the justice shall, in the presence of the accused, before asking the accused if he wishes to call witnesses, (a) cause the deposition to be read to the witness; (b) cause the deposition to be signed by the witness; and (c) sign the deposition himself.
-- src:12008 | (2) Where a deposition is taken down in writing, the justice shall, in the presence of the accused, before asking the accused if he wishes to call witnesses,
-- src:12009 | (a) cause the deposition to be read to the witness;
-- src:12010 | (b) cause the deposition to be signed by the witness; and
-- src:12011 | (c) sign the deposition himself.
@ref s 540(2) (src:12008-12011)
DECLARE `s 540(2) the step` IS ONE OF
    `s 540(2)(a) cause the deposition to be read to the witness`
    `s 540(2)(b) cause the deposition to be signed by the witness`
    `s 540(2)(c) sign the deposition himself`
    `s 540(2) any other step`

-- src:12008 | (2) Where a deposition is taken down in writing, the justice shall, in the presence of the accused, before asking the accused if he wishes to call witnesses,
-- src:12009 | (a) cause the deposition to be read to the witness;
-- src:12010 | (b) cause the deposition to be signed by the witness; and
-- src:12011 | (c) sign the deposition himself.
@ref s 540(2) (src:12008-12011)
GIVEN `a deposition is taken down in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice has asked the accused if the accused wishes to call witnesses` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the step` IS A `s 540(2) the step`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 540(2) the justice shall, in the presence of the accused, take the step before asking the accused if the accused wishes to call witnesses` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a deposition is taken down in writing` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a deposition is taken down in writing"
        IF `the step` EQUALS `s 540(2) any other step` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "the justice shall, in the presence of the accused, before asking the accused if he wishes to call witnesses"
        IF `the justice has asked the accused if the accused wishes to call witnesses` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "before asking the accused if he wishes to call witnesses"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 540 (3) Where depositions are taken down in writing, the justice may sign (a) at the end of each deposition; or (b) at the end of several or of all the depositions in a manner that will indicate that his signature is intended to authenticate each deposition.
