      `the justice signs at the end of each deposition, or at the end of several or of all in a manner that indicates the signature is intended to authenticate each` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 540(3) the justice may sign at the end of each deposition or at the end of several or of all of them` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `depositions are taken down in writing` THEN JUST FALSE   -- GRANT-GATE: where/when/upon/period -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where depositions are taken down in writing"
        IF NOT `the justice signs at the end of each deposition, or at the end of several or of all in a manner that indicates the signature is intended to authenticate each` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in a manner that will indicate that his signature is intended to authenticate each deposition"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 540 (4) Where the stenographer appointed to take down the evidence is not a duly sworn court stenographer, he shall make oath that he will truly and faithfully report the evidence.
-- src:12017 | (4) Where the stenographer appointed to take down the evidence is not a duly sworn court stenographer, he shall make oath that he will truly and faithfully report the evidence.
@ref s 540(4) (src:12017-12017)
GIVEN `a stenographer is appointed to take down the evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the stenographer is a duly sworn court stenographer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 540(4) the stenographer shall make oath that they will truly and faithfully report the evidence` MEANS
    IF `a stenographer is appointed to take down the evidence` AND NOT `the stenographer is a duly sworn court stenographer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the stenographer appointed to take down the evidence is not a duly sworn court stenographer"

-- 540 (5) Where the evidence is taken down by a stenographer appointed by the justice or pursuant to law, it need not be read to or signed by the witnesses, but, on request of the justice or of one of the parties, shall be transcribed, in whole or in part,
