      `the justice or one of the parties requests a transcript` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 540(5) the stenographer shall transcribe the evidence, in whole or in part` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the evidence is taken down by a stenographer appointed by the justice or pursuant to law` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the evidence is taken down by a stenographer appointed by the justice or pursuant to law"
        IF NOT `the justice or one of the parties requests a transcript` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on request of the justice or of one of the parties"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:12020 | (a) an affidavit of the stenographer that it is a true report of the evidence; or
