§§ `Section 541 -- Hearing of witnesses`

-- 541 (1) When the evidence of the witnesses called on the part of the prosecution has been taken down and, if required by this Part, has been read, the justice shall, subject to this section and subsection 537(1.01), hear the witnesses called by the accused.
-- src:12031 | 541 (1) When the evidence of the witnesses called on the part of the prosecution has been taken down and, if required by this Part, has been read, the justice shall, subject to this section and subsection 537(1.01), hear the witnesses called by the accused.
@ref s 541(1) (src:12031-12031)
GIVEN `the evidence of the witnesses called on the part of the prosecution has been taken down and, if required by this Part, has been read` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice has limited the witnesses to be heard under subsection 537(1.01)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 541(1) the justice shall hear the witnesses called by the accused` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the evidence of the witnesses called on the part of the prosecution has been taken down and, if required by this Part, has been read` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When the evidence of the witnesses called on the part of the prosecution has been taken down"
        IF `the justice has limited the witnesses to be heard under subsection 537(1.01)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to this section and subsection 537(1.01)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 541 (2) Before hearing any witness called by an accused who is not represented by counsel, the justice shall address the accused as follows or to the like effect: (the words)
-- src:12034 | “Do you wish to say anything in answer to these charges or to any other charges which might have arisen from the evidence led by the prosecution? You are not obliged to say anything, but whatever you do say may be given in evidence against you at your trial. You should not make any confession or admission of guilt because of any promise or threat made to you but if you do make any statement it may be given in evidence against you at your trial in spite of the promise or threat.”
@ref s 541(2) (src:12034-12034)
`s 541(2) the words in which the justice addresses the accused` MEANS "“Do you wish to say anything in answer to these charges or to any other charges which might have arisen from the evidence led by the prosecution? You are not obliged to say anything, but whatever you do say may be given in evidence against you at your trial. You should not make any confession or admission of guilt because of any promise or threat made to you but if you do make any statement it may be given in evidence against you at your trial in spite of the promise or threat.”"

-- src:12033 | (2) Before hearing any witness called by an accused who is not represented by counsel, the justice shall address the accused as follows or to the like effect:
@ref s 541(2) (src:12033-12033)
GIVEN `the accused is represented by counsel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice has begun to hear a witness called by the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 541(2) the justice shall address the accused in the words of subsection (2)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the accused is represented by counsel` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an accused who is not represented by counsel"
        IF `the justice has begun to hear a witness called by the accused` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Before hearing any witness called by an accused"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 541 (3) Where the accused who is not represented by counsel says anything in answer to the address made by the justice pursuant to subsection (2), the answer shall be taken down in writing and shall be signed by the justice and kept with the evidence
-- of the witnesses and dealt with in accordance with this Part.
-- src:12036 | (3) Where the accused who is not represented by counsel says anything in answer to the address made by the justice pursuant to subsection (2), the answer shall be taken down in writing and shall be signed by the justice and kept with the evidence of the witnesses and dealt with in accordance with this Part.
@ref s 541(3) (src:12036-12036)
GIVEN `the accused is represented by counsel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused says anything in answer to the address made by the justice pursuant to subsection 541(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 541(3) the answer shall be taken down in writing, signed by the justice and kept with the evidence of the witnesses` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the accused is represented by counsel` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the accused who is not represented by counsel says anything in answer to the address"
        IF NOT `the accused says anything in answer to the address made by the justice pursuant to subsection 541(2)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "says anything in answer to the address made by the justice pursuant to subsection (2)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 541 (4) Where an accused is not represented by counsel, the justice shall ask the accused if he or she wishes to call any witnesses after subsections (2) and (3) have been complied with.
-- src:12038 | (4) Where an accused is not represented by counsel, the justice shall ask the accused if he or she wishes to call any witnesses after subsections (2) and (3) have been complied with.
@ref s 541(4) (src:12038-12038)
GIVEN `the accused is represented by counsel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsections 541(2) and (3) have been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 541(4) the justice shall ask the accused if the accused wishes to call any witnesses` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the accused is represented by counsel` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an accused is not represented by counsel"
        IF NOT `subsections 541(2) and (3) have been complied with` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "after subsections (2) and (3) have been complied with"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 541 (5) Subject to subsection 537(1.01), the justice shall hear each witness called by the accused who testifies to any matter relevant to the inquiry, and for the purposes of this subsection, section 540 applies with any modifications that the circumstances require.
-- src:12040 | (5) Subject to subsection 537(1.01), the justice shall hear each witness called by the accused who testifies to any matter relevant to the inquiry, and for the purposes of this subsection, section 540 applies with any modifications that the circumstances require.
@ref s 541(5) (src:12040-12040)
GIVEN `the witness is called by the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the witness testifies to a matter relevant to the inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice has limited the witnesses to be heard under subsection 537(1.01)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 541(5) the justice shall hear the witness` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the witness is called by the accused` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "each witness called by the accused"
        IF NOT `the witness testifies to a matter relevant to the inquiry` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who testifies to any matter relevant to the inquiry"
        IF `the justice has limited the witnesses to be heard under subsection 537(1.01)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to subsection 537(1.01)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:12040 | (5) Subject to subsection 537(1.01), the justice shall hear each witness called by the accused who testifies to any matter relevant to the inquiry, and for the purposes of this subsection, section 540 applies with any modifications that the circumstances require.
@ref s 541(5) (src:12040-12040)
GIVEN `the answer of s 541(5) the justice shall hear the witness` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 541(5) section 540 applies with any modifications that the circumstances require to the hearing of the witness` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer of s 541(5) the justice shall hear the witness`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the purposes of this subsection": there is no hearing of the witness under this subsection
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the purposes of this subsection"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE

§§ `Section 542 -- Confession or admission of accused`

-- 542 (1) Nothing in this Act prevents a prosecutor giving in evidence at a preliminary inquiry any admission, confession or statement made at any time by the accused that by law is admissible against him.
-- src:12042 | 542 (1) Nothing in this Act prevents a prosecutor giving in evidence at a preliminary inquiry any admission, confession or statement made at any time by the accused that by law is admissible against him.
@ref s 542(1) (src:12042-12042)
GIVEN `the admission, confession or statement made at any time by the accused is by law admissible against the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 542(1) the prosecutor may give the admission, confession or statement in evidence at the preliminary inquiry` MEANS
    IF `the admission, confession or statement made at any time by the accused is by law admissible against the accused`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that by law is admissible against him"

-- 542 (2) Every one who publishes in any document, or broadcasts or transmits in any way, a report that any admission or confession was tendered in evidence at a preliminary inquiry or a report of the nature of such admission or confession so tendered in evidence
-- unless (a) the accused has been discharged, or (b) if the accused has been ordered to stand trial, the trial has ended, is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
-- src:12044 | (2) Every one who publishes in any document, or broadcasts or transmits in any way, a report that any admission or confession was tendered in evidence at a preliminary inquiry or a report of the nature of such admission or confession so tendered in evidence unless
-- src:12045 | (a) the accused has been discharged, or
-- src:12046 | (b) if the accused has been ordered to stand trial, the trial has ended,
-- src:12047 | is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 542(2) (src:12044-12047)
GIVEN `the person publishes in any document, or broadcasts or transmits in any way, a report that an admission or confession was tendered in evidence at a preliminary inquiry or a report of the nature of such an admission or confession` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused has been discharged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused has been ordered to stand trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trial has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 542(2) the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person publishes in any document, or broadcasts or transmits in any way, a report that an admission or confession was tendered in evidence at a preliminary inquiry or a report of the nature of such an admission or confession` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one who publishes in any document, or broadcasts or transmits in any way, a report that any admission or confession was tendered in evidence at a preliminary inquiry"
        IF `the accused has been discharged` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless (a) the accused has been discharged"
        IF `the accused has been ordered to stand trial` AND `the trial has ended` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the accused has been ordered to stand trial, the trial has ended"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:12047 | is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 542(2) (src:12047-12047)
`s 542(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:12047 | is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 542(2) (src:12047-12047)
`s 542(2) the punishment the section states` MEANS
    Punishment WITH
        `mode` IS `on summary conviction`
        `maximum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`
        `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`
        `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`
        `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`

-- 542 (3) [Repealed, 2005, c. 32, s. 19]: the text shows
-- src:12048 | (3) [Repealed, 2005, c. 32, s. 19]
@ref s 542(3) (src:12048-12048)
`s 542(3) repealed` MEANS "(3) [Repealed, 2005, c. 32, s. 19]"

§§ `Section 543 -- Remand where offence committed in another jurisdiction`

-- 543 (1) If an accused is charged with an offence alleged to have been committed out of the limits of the jurisdiction in which they have been charged, the justice before whom they appear or are brought may, at any stage of the inquiry after hearing both parties,
-- order the accused to appear or, if the accused is in custody, issue a warrant in Form 15 to convey the accused before a justice who, having jurisdiction in the place where the offence is alleged to have been committed, shall continue and complete the inquiry.
-- src:12052 | 543 (1) If an accused is charged with an offence alleged to have been committed out of the limits of the jurisdiction in which they have been charged, the justice before whom they appear or are brought may, at any stage of the inquiry after hearing both parties, order the accused to appear or, if the accused is in custody, issue a warrant in Form 15 to convey the accused before a justice who, having jurisdiction in the place where the offence is alleged to have been committed, shall continue and complete the inquiry.
@ref s 543(1) (src:12052-12052)
GIVEN `the offence is alleged to have been committed out of the limits of the jurisdiction in which the accused has been charged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `both parties have been heard` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 543(1) the justice may order the accused to appear before a justice in the place where the offence is alleged to have been committed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the offence is alleged to have been committed out of the limits of the jurisdiction in which the accused has been charged` THEN NOTHING   -- GRANT-GATE: if -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If an accused is charged with an offence alleged to have been committed out of the limits of the jurisdiction in which they have been charged"
        IF NOT `both parties have been heard` THEN JUST FALSE   -- GRANT-GATE: where/when/upon/period -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at any stage of the inquiry after hearing both parties"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:12052 | 543 (1) If an accused is charged with an offence alleged to have been committed out of the limits of the jurisdiction in which they have been charged, the justice before whom they appear or are brought may, at any stage of the inquiry after hearing both parties, order the accused to appear or, if the accused is in custody, issue a warrant in Form 15 to convey the accused before a justice who, having jurisdiction in the place where the offence is alleged to have been committed, shall continue and complete the inquiry.
@ref s 543(1) (src:12052-12052)
GIVEN `the answer of s 543(1) the justice may order the accused to appear` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the accused is in custody` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 543(1) the justice may issue a warrant in Form 15 to convey the accused` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer of s 543(1) the justice may order the accused to appear`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the justice may make the order is not settled
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- GRANT-GATE: where/when/upon/period -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at any stage of the inquiry after hearing both parties"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the accused is in custody`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING   -- GRANT-GATE: if -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the accused is in custody, issue a warrant in Form 15"

-- src:12052 | 543 (1) If an accused is charged with an offence alleged to have been committed out of the limits of the jurisdiction in which they have been charged, the justice before whom they appear or are brought may, at any stage of the inquiry after hearing both parties, order the accused to appear or, if the accused is in custody, issue a warrant in Form 15 to convey the accused before a justice who, having jurisdiction in the place where the offence is alleged to have been committed, shall continue and complete the inquiry.
@ref s 543(1) (src:12052-12052)
GIVEN `the justice has jurisdiction in the place where the offence is alleged to have been committed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 543(1) the justice in the place where the offence is alleged to have been committed shall continue and complete the inquiry` MEANS
    IF `the justice has jurisdiction in the place where the offence is alleged to have been committed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a justice who, having jurisdiction in the place where the offence is alleged to have been committed"

-- 543 (2) Where a justice makes an order or issues a warrant pursuant to subsection (1), he shall cause the transcript of any evidence given before him in the inquiry and all documents that were then before him and that are relevant to the inquiry to be transmitted to a justice
-- having jurisdiction in the place where the offence is alleged to have been committed and (a) any evidence the transcript of which is so transmitted shall be deemed to have been taken by the justice to whom it is transmitted; and (b) any appearance notice, undertaking or release order ...
-- src:12054 | (2) Where a justice makes an order or issues a warrant pursuant to subsection (1), he shall cause the transcript of any evidence given before him in the inquiry and all documents that were then before him and that are relevant to the inquiry to be transmitted to a justice having jurisdiction in the place where the offence is alleged to have been committed and
@ref s 543(2) (src:12054-12054)
GIVEN `the justice makes an order or issues a warrant pursuant to subsection 543(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 543(2) the justice shall cause the transcript and the relevant documents to be transmitted to a justice having jurisdiction in the place where the offence is alleged to have been committed` MEANS
    IF `the justice makes an order or issues a warrant pursuant to subsection 543(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a justice makes an order or issues a warrant pursuant to subsection (1)"

-- src:12055 | (a) any evidence the transcript of which is so transmitted shall be deemed to have been taken by the justice to whom it is transmitted; and
@ref s 543(2)(a) (src:12055-12055)
GIVEN `the answer of s 543(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the transcript of the evidence has been so transmitted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 543(2)(a) the evidence is deemed to have been taken by the justice to whom it is transmitted` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer of s 543(2)`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether an order was made or a warrant issued is not settled
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a justice makes an order or issues a warrant pursuant to subsection (1)"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the transcript of the evidence has been so transmitted`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any evidence the transcript of which is so transmitted"

-- src:12056 | (b) any appearance notice, undertaking or release order issued to or given or entered into by the accused shall be deemed to have been issued, given or entered into in the jurisdiction where the offence is alleged to have been committed and to require the accused to appear before the justice to whom the transcript and documents are transmitted at the time provided in the order made in respect of the accused under paragraph (1)(a).
@ref s 543(2)(b) (src:12056-12056)
GIVEN `the answer of s 543(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the document` IS A `Process document`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 543(2)(b) the document is deemed to have been issued, given or entered into in the jurisdiction where the offence is alleged to have been committed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the answer of s 543(2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a justice makes an order or issues a warrant pursuant to subsection (1)"
        IF `the answer of s 543(2)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether an order was made or a warrant issued is not settled
        IF `the document` EQUALS `an appearance notice` OR `the document` EQUALS `an undertaking` OR `the document` EQUALS `a release order` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any appearance notice, undertaking or release order"

§§ `Section 544 -- Absconding accused`

-- 544 (1) Notwithstanding any other provision of this Act, where an accused, whether or not he is charged jointly with another, absconds during the course of a preliminary inquiry into an offence with which he is charged, (a) he shall be deemed to have waived his right to be present at the inquiry, and
-- src:12060 | 544 (1) Notwithstanding any other provision of this Act, where an accused, whether or not he is charged jointly with another, absconds during the course of a preliminary inquiry into an offence with which he is charged,
-- src:12061 | (a) he shall be deemed to have waived his right to be present at the inquiry, and
@ref s 544(1)(a) (src:12060-12061)
