GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 544(1)(b)(i) the justice may continue the inquiry` MEANS
    IF `the accused absconds during the course of a preliminary inquiry into an offence with which the accused is charged`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- GRANT-GATE: where/when/upon/period -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where an accused, whether or not he is charged jointly with another, absconds during the course of a preliminary inquiry"

-- src:12063 | (i) may continue the inquiry and, when all the evidence has been taken, shall dispose of the inquiry in accordance with section 548, or
