-- src:12123 | (3) A justice may, for any reason satisfactory to him, require any witness entering into a recognizance pursuant to this section
-- src:12124 | (a) to produce one or more sureties in such amount as he may direct; or
-- src:12125 | (b) to deposit with him a sum of money sufficient in his opinion to ensure that the witness will appear and give evidence.
@ref s 550(3) (src:12123-12125)
GIVEN `the witness is entering into a recognizance pursuant to section 550` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice has a reason satisfactory to the justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 550(3) the justice may require the witness to produce sureties or to deposit a sum of money` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the witness is entering into a recognizance pursuant to section 550` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any witness entering into a recognizance pursuant to this section"
        IF NOT `the justice has a reason satisfactory to the justice` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for any reason satisfactory to him"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 550 (4) Where a witness does not comply with subsection (1) or (3) when required to do so by a justice, he may be committed by the justice, by warrant in Form 24, to a prison in the territorial division where the trial is to be held,
-- there to be kept until he does what is required of him or until the trial is concluded.
-- src:12127 | (4) Where a witness does not comply with subsection (1) or (3) when required to do so by a justice, he may be committed by the justice, by warrant in Form 24, to a prison in the territorial division where the trial is to be held, there to be kept until he does what is required of him or until the trial is concluded.
@ref s 550(4) (src:12127-12127)
GIVEN `the witness does not comply with subsection 550(1) or (3) when required to do so by a justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 550(4) the witness may be committed by warrant in Form 24 to a prison in the territorial division where the trial is to be held` MEANS
    IF `the witness does not comply with subsection 550(1) or (3) when required to do so by a justice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- GRANT-GATE: where/when/upon/period -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a witness does not comply with subsection (1) or (3) when required to do so by a justice"

-- "there to be kept until he does what is required of him or until the trial is concluded": an "until" bar (ruling (d) of 2026-11-05): JUST TRUE while the witness may be kept, JUST FALSE once either has happened.
-- src:12127 | (4) Where a witness does not comply with subsection (1) or (3) when required to do so by a justice, he may be committed by the justice, by warrant in Form 24, to a prison in the territorial division where the trial is to be held, there to be kept until he does what is required of him or until the trial is concluded.
@ref s 550(4) (src:12127-12127)
GIVEN `the witness has been committed under subsection 550(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the witness has done what is required of them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trial is concluded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 550(4) the witness may still be kept in prison` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the witness has been committed under subsection 550(4)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- GRANT-GATE: where/when/upon/period -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "he may be committed by the justice, by warrant in Form 24, to a prison"
        IF `the witness has done what is required of them` THEN JUST FALSE   -- GRANT-GATE: where/when/upon/period -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until he does what is required of him"
        IF `the trial is concluded` THEN JUST FALSE   -- GRANT-GATE: where/when/upon/period -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until the trial is concluded"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 550 (5) Where a witness has been committed to prison pursuant to subsection (4), the court before which the witness appears or a justice having jurisdiction in the territorial division where the prison is situated may, by order in Form 39, discharge the witness from custody when the trial is concluded.
-- src:12129 | (5) Where a witness has been committed to prison pursuant to subsection (4), the court before which the witness appears or a justice having jurisdiction in the territorial division where the prison is situated may, by order in Form 39, discharge the witness from custody when the trial is concluded.
@ref s 550(5) (src:12129-12129)
GIVEN `the witness has been committed to prison pursuant to subsection 550(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trial is concluded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 550(5) the court or a justice may by order in Form 39 discharge the witness from custody` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the witness has been committed to prison pursuant to subsection 550(4)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- GRANT-GATE: where/when/upon/period -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a witness has been committed to prison pursuant to subsection (4)"
        IF NOT `the trial is concluded` THEN JUST FALSE   -- GRANT-GATE: where/when/upon/period -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when the trial is concluded"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Section 551 -- Transmission of record`

-- 551 If a justice orders an accused to stand trial, the justice shall immediately send to the clerk or other proper officer of the court by which the accused is to be tried, any information, evidence, exhibits, or statement of the accused taken down in writing in accordance with section 541,
-- any appearance notice, undertaking or release order given by or issued to the accused and any evidence taken before a coroner that is in the possession of the justice.
-- src:12133 | 551 If a justice orders an accused to stand trial, the justice shall immediately send to the clerk or other proper officer of the court by which the accused is to be tried, any information, evidence, exhibits, or statement of the accused taken down in writing in accordance with section 541, any appearance notice, undertaking or release order given by or issued to the accused and any evidence taken before a coroner that is in the possession of the justice.
@ref s 551 (src:12133-12133)
DECLARE `s 551 the item` IS ONE OF
    `s 551 an information`
    `s 551 evidence`
    `s 551 exhibits`
    `s 551 a statement of the accused taken down in writing in accordance with section 541`
    `s 551 an appearance notice, undertaking or release order given by or issued to the accused`
    `s 551 evidence taken before a coroner`
    `s 551 anything else`

-- src:12133 | 551 If a justice orders an accused to stand trial, the justice shall immediately send to the clerk or other proper officer of the court by which the accused is to be tried, any information, evidence, exhibits, or statement of the accused taken down in writing in accordance with section 541, any appearance notice, undertaking or release order given by or issued to the accused and any evidence taken before a coroner that is in the possession of the justice.
@ref s 551 (src:12133-12133)
GIVEN `the justice orders the accused to stand trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the item` IS A `s 551 the item`
      `the evidence taken before a coroner is in the possession of the justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 551 the justice shall immediately send the item to the clerk or other proper officer of the court by which the accused is to be tried` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the justice orders the accused to stand trial` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a justice orders an accused to stand trial"
        IF `the item` EQUALS `s 551 anything else` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "any information, evidence, exhibits, or statement of the accused"
        IF `the item` EQUALS `s 551 evidence taken before a coroner` AND NOT `the evidence taken before a coroner is in the possession of the justice` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any evidence taken before a coroner that is in the possession of the justice"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Regulative rules of Part XVIII (parties, order and time, where the text gives them)`

-- 536.3: the prosecutor, or counsel for the accused if the accused made the request, shall provide the statement within the period fixed by rules of court or, if none, by the justice. The number of days is an input; time 0 is the request.
-- src:11946 | 536.3 If a request for a preliminary inquiry is made, the prosecutor or, if the request was made by the accused, counsel for the accused shall, within the period fixed by rules of court made under section 482 or 482.1 or, if there are no such rules, by the justice, provide the court and the other party with a statement that identifies
@ref s 536.3 (src:11946-11946)
DECLARE `s 536.3 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 536.3 provides the court and the other party with the statement`

-- src:11946 | 536.3 If a request for a preliminary inquiry is made, the prosecutor or, if the request was made by the accused, counsel for the accused shall, within the period fixed by rules of court made under section 482 or 482.1 or, if there are no such rules, by the justice, provide the court and the other party with a statement that identifies
@ref s 536.3 (src:11946-11946)
GIVEN `the period fixed, in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 536.3 action`
`s 536.3 the prosecutor must provide the statement within the period fixed` MEANS
    PARTY `the prosecutor`
    MUST `s 536.3 provides the court and the other party with the statement`
    WITHIN `the period fixed, in days`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the prosecutor did not provide the statement within the period fixed by rules of court or, if there are no such rules, by the justice"

-- src:11946 | 536.3 If a request for a preliminary inquiry is made, the prosecutor or, if the request was made by the accused, counsel for the accused shall, within the period fixed by rules of court made under section 482 or 482.1 or, if there are no such rules, by the justice, provide the court and the other party with a statement that identifies
@ref s 536.3 (src:11946-11946)
GIVEN `the period fixed, in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 536.3 action`
`s 536.3 counsel for the accused must provide the statement within the period fixed` MEANS
    PARTY `counsel for the accused`
    MUST `s 536.3 provides the court and the other party with the statement`
    WITHIN `the period fixed, in days`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "counsel for the accused did not provide the statement within the period fixed by rules of court or, if there are no such rules, by the justice"

-- 541(2), (4) and (5): for an accused with no counsel, the justice addresses the accused, then asks if the accused wishes to call witnesses, then hears each witness. The text gives the order and no number of days.
-- src:12033 | (2) Before hearing any witness called by an accused who is not represented by counsel, the justice shall address the accused as follows or to the like effect:
-- src:12034 | “Do you wish to say anything in answer to these charges or to any other charges which might have arisen from the evidence led by the prosecution? You are not obliged to say anything, but whatever you do say may be given in evidence against you at your trial. You should not make any confession or admission of guilt because of any promise or threat made to you but if you do make any statement it may be given in evidence against you at your trial in spite of the promise or threat.”
-- src:12035 | Statement of accused
-- src:12036 | (3) Where the accused who is not represented by counsel says anything in answer to the address made by the justice pursuant to subsection (2), the answer shall be taken down in writing and shall be signed by the justice and kept with the evidence of the witnesses and dealt with in accordance with this Part.
-- src:12037 | Witnesses for accused
-- src:12038 | (4) Where an accused is not represented by counsel, the justice shall ask the accused if he or she wishes to call any witnesses after subsections (2) and (3) have been complied with.
-- src:12039 | Depositions of witnesses
-- src:12040 | (5) Subject to subsection 537(1.01), the justice shall hear each witness called by the accused who testifies to any matter relevant to the inquiry, and for the purposes of this subsection, section 540 applies with any modifications that the circumstances require.
@ref s 541 (src:12033-12040)
DECLARE `s 541 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 541(2) addresses the accused in the words of subsection (2)`
    `s 541(4) asks the accused if the accused wishes to call any witnesses`
    `s 541(5) hears each witness called by the accused`

-- src:12033 | (2) Before hearing any witness called by an accused who is not represented by counsel, the justice shall address the accused as follows or to the like effect:
-- src:12034 | “Do you wish to say anything in answer to these charges or to any other charges which might have arisen from the evidence led by the prosecution? You are not obliged to say anything, but whatever you do say may be given in evidence against you at your trial. You should not make any confession or admission of guilt because of any promise or threat made to you but if you do make any statement it may be given in evidence against you at your trial in spite of the promise or threat.”
-- src:12035 | Statement of accused
-- src:12036 | (3) Where the accused who is not represented by counsel says anything in answer to the address made by the justice pursuant to subsection (2), the answer shall be taken down in writing and shall be signed by the justice and kept with the evidence of the witnesses and dealt with in accordance with this Part.
-- src:12037 | Witnesses for accused
-- src:12038 | (4) Where an accused is not represented by counsel, the justice shall ask the accused if he or she wishes to call any witnesses after subsections (2) and (3) have been complied with.
-- src:12039 | Depositions of witnesses
-- src:12040 | (5) Subject to subsection 537(1.01), the justice shall hear each witness called by the accused who testifies to any matter relevant to the inquiry, and for the purposes of this subsection, section 540 applies with any modifications that the circumstances require.
@ref s 541 (src:12033-12040)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 541 action`
`s 541 the justice must address the unrepresented accused, ask about witnesses, and hear them` MEANS
    PARTY `a justice`
    MUST `s 541(2) addresses the accused in the words of subsection (2)`
    HENCE
        PARTY `a justice`
        MUST `s 541(4) asks the accused if the accused wishes to call any witnesses`
        HENCE
            PARTY `a justice`
            MUST `s 541(5) hears each witness called by the accused`
            HENCE FULFILLED

-- 551: if a justice orders the accused to stand trial, the justice shall immediately send the record to the clerk of the court by which the accused is to be tried. "Immediately" is not a number, so there is no WITHIN.
-- src:12133 | 551 If a justice orders an accused to stand trial, the justice shall immediately send to the clerk or other proper officer of the court by which the accused is to be tried, any information, evidence, exhibits, or statement of the accused taken down in writing in accordance with section 541, any appearance notice, undertaking or release order given by or issued to the accused and any evidence taken before a coroner that is in the possession of the justice.
@ref s 551 (src:12133-12133)
DECLARE `s 551 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 551 sends the record to the clerk or other proper officer of the court by which the accused is to be tried`

-- src:12133 | 551 If a justice orders an accused to stand trial, the justice shall immediately send to the clerk or other proper officer of the court by which the accused is to be tried, any information, evidence, exhibits, or statement of the accused taken down in writing in accordance with section 541, any appearance notice, undertaking or release order given by or issued to the accused and any evidence taken before a coroner that is in the possession of the justice.
@ref s 551 (src:12133-12133)
